0,Mewari language - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mewari_language,"Mewari is an Indo-Aryan language of the Rajasthani languages group. [2] It is spoken by about five million speakers in Rajsamand, Bhilwara, Udaipur, Chittorgarh and Pratapgarh districts of Rajasthan state and Mandsaur, Neemuch districts of Madhya Pradesh state of India.",Mewari,Indo-European
1,Indo-European languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Indo-European_languages,"The Indo-European family is significant to the field of historical linguistics as it possesses the second-longest recorded history of any known family after Egyptian and the Semitic languages, which belong to the Afroasiatic language family.",Mewari,Indo-European
2,The Sound of Indo-European Music (Compilation) - YouTube,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=WgHSW774Q-4,"In this video, I compiled music from all the major Indo-European languages. I hope you enjoy these great songs!",Mewari,Indo-European
3,"Mewari Language (MTR) - L1 & L2 Speakers, Status, Map, Endangered Level ...",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/mtr/,"Mewari is a stable indigenous language of India. It belongs to the Indo-European language family and is part of the Marwari macrolanguage. Direct evidence is lacking, but the language is thought to be used as a first language by all in the ethnic community. It is not known to be taught in schools.",Mewari,Indo-European
